      "line_start": 288,
      "line_end": 313,
      "observation": "Held Durrett p. 88 (pdf 96), the opening of section 2.5.2 inside the chapter's cited pp. 87-90 extent, asserts for the St. Petersburg game that S_n/(n log_2 n) -> 1 in probability but limsup S_n/(n log_2 n) = infinity almost surely (pointing to Exercise 2.3.20), and attributes Theorem 2.5.13 to Feller (1946). The almost-sure limsup statement is not stated, proved or routed in this chapter or its boundary; grep finds no Exercise 2.3.20 anywhere under handbook/parts/p15 or handbook/annex/p15. Thm p15-rate-calculated-examples item 4 uses the same law only with a_n = n and a_n = n^2. No owed component's exact text promises this statement, so no verdict changes. The gap belongs to whichever unit owns Durrett Exercise 2.3.20 or the section 2.5.2 preamble.",
      "affects_verdict": false
    },
    {
      "component_id": "ED26-P15-CH-infinite-mean-weak-normalization-C013",
